{
  "$comment": "DDD bridge for Glossy, the design system glossy-portfolio-theme defines for itself (design-system/glossy.tokens.json, a local source). Tiers follow elements/d-d-d/design-system/bridge/contract.json. Glossy is dark by design, so every named DDD color points at one fixed studio or glass color: white is the ink and coalyGray is the card panel, the pair DDD blocks use on a dark page. Links in content are told apart from the text around them by an underline, not by color alone (lib/GlossyContentStyles.js), since glass cyan on white text cannot reach 3:1. Kept as DDD on purpose: font weights, state opacities, control heights and border widths, and heading sizes. Body text is 16px, the size the theme's rem-based chrome and pages were drawn at.",
  "system": "glossy",
  "title": "Glossy",
  "prefix": "Glossy",
  "colorNames": {
    "strip": ["--glossy-studio-", "--glossy-glass-", "--glossy-"]
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/haxtheweb/webcomponents/tree/master/elements/glossy-portfolio-theme",
  "sources": [
    {
      "local": true,
      "file": "design-system/glossy.tokens.json",
      "format": "dtcg",
      "prefix": "--glossy-",
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "copyright": "Copyright 2026 The Pennsylvania State University"
    }
  ],
  "fonts": [
    {
      "family": "Manrope",
      "license": "OFL-1.1"
    },
    {
      "family": "Inter",
      "license": "OFL-1.1"
